_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 1
---
order: 1
---
short_label: VII.1
---
statement: When two unequal numbers are set out, and the less is continually subtracted in turn from the greater, if the number which is left never measures the one before it until a unit is left, then the original numbers are relatively prime.
---
red_highlight: yes
---
proof:

The less of two unequal numbers *AB* and *CD* being continually subtracted from the greater, let the number which is left never measure the one before it until a unit is left.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="140" height="270" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VII.1 diagram" src="propVII1.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
